---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Help" description="How Denver Social works — for attendees, organizers, and group hosts.">
  <div class="hp">
    <header class="hp-h">
      <p class="hp-kicker">Help</p>
      <h1>How this works.</h1>
      <p class="hp-lede">Short answers for everyone — attendees, organizers, group hosts. If you can't find what you need, <a href="/contact">send us a note</a>.</p>
    </header>

    <nav class="hp-toc" aria-label="Sections">
      <a href="#attendees">Attending</a>
      <a href="#organizers">Hosting</a>
      <a href="#groups">Groups</a>
      <a href="#reporting">Reporting</a>
      <a href="#safety">Safety</a>
      <a href="#account">Account</a>
    </nav>

    <section class="hp-s" id="attendees">
      <h2>Attending</h2>
      <details class="hp-q">
        <summary>How do I RSVP to an event?</summary>
        <div class="hp-a"><p>Find one on <a href="/events">/events</a>, open it, hit RSVP. You'll need a free email-code sign-in so the host knows who's coming.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="hp-q">
        <summary>What do I bring?</summary>
        <div class="hp-a"><p>Depends on the event — the page tells you. Potlucks ask you to claim a dish slot. Otherwise, just yourself.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="hp-q">
        <summary>How do I cancel an RSVP?</summary>
        <div class="hp-a"><p>From <a href="/profile">/profile</a>, find the event, hit Cancel. Cancel early so the spot can go to the waitlist.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="hp-q">
        <summary>Where are events?</summary>
        <div class="hp-a"><p>Across Denver metro — RiNo, Cap Hill, Cheesman, Cherry Creek, Highland, the foothills. The full address is on every event page.</p></div>
      </details>
    </section>

    <section class="hp-s" id="organizers">
      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <details class="hp-q">
        <summary>How do I post an event?</summary>
        <div class="hp-a"><p>Sign in, then <a href="/events/new">/events/new</a>. Pick a type, name it, set the date, fill in the details, post.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="hp-q">
        <summary>Can I run a potluck?</summary>
        <div class="hp-a"><p>Yes — anyone can. Head to <a href="/potlucks/new">/potlucks/new</a>. We'll generate the sign-up sheet and the public link.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="hp-q">
        <summary>How do I cap attendance?</summary>
        <div class="hp-a"><p>Set a "spots" number when you post. Once it fills, new RSVPs go to a waitlist. If someone cancels, the next person up gets promoted automatically.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="hp-q">
        <summary>Are reminders sent automatically?</summary>
        <div class="hp-a"><p>Day-before email reminders for potlucks go out automatically when an event date is set. Other event types don't have reminders yet.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="hp-q">
        <summary>How do I delete an event?</summary>
        <div class="hp-a"><p>Open the event, hit the red 🗑 Delete button at the top. Wipes RSVPs, comments, and bring-items. Cannot be undone.</p></div>
      </details>
    </section>

    <section class="hp-s" id="groups">
      <h2>Groups</h2>
      <details class="hp-q">
        <summary>What's a group?</summary>
        <div class="hp-a"><p>A smaller circle inside Denver Social — your hiking buddies, trivia crew, dinner club. Anyone can start one and post events scoped to it.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="hp-q">
        <summary>Public vs invite-only?</summary>
        <div class="hp-a"><p>Public: anyone signed in can find it at <a href="/groups">/groups</a> and join. Invite-only: people join via a single-use invite link from a member.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="hp-q">
        <summary>How do I post in a group?</summary>
        <div class="hp-a"><p>From the group page, hit "+ New event". It'll be tagged with the group but still appear on the main events list.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="hp-q">
        <summary>How do I leave?</summary>
        <div class="hp-a"><p>Open the group, hit Leave. Owners need to transfer ownership before leaving — message us if you need help.</p></div>
      </details>
    </section>

    <section class="hp-s" id="reporting">
      <h2>Reporting</h2>
      <details class="hp-q">
        <summary>How do I report someone or something?</summary>
        <div class="hp-a">
          <p>Hit the 🚩 Report button on any event, group, or profile page. Pick a reason, add a note, submit. An admin reviews it and either acts (warning, content removed, account suspended) or dismisses it. We don't tell the reported person who flagged them.</p>
          <p>You don't need proof — if it made you uncomfortable, that's reason enough.</p>
          <p><strong>Emergency?</strong> Call 911 first. Message us after you're safe.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </section>

    <section class="hp-s" id="safety">
      <h2>Safety</h2>
      <ul class="hp-rules">
        <li><strong>Everyone's welcome.</strong> Quiet, loud, awkward, neurodivergent, brand new to Denver. Leave whenever — no explanation needed.</li>
        <li><strong>Your info stays private.</strong> Host phone numbers stay hidden until you ask and they approve. Other members see your first name and neighborhood, nothing else.</li>
        <li><strong>Hosts are accountable.</strong> Every event has a named host. Admin can take any page offline at any time.</li>
        <li><strong>What gets you removed.</strong> Harassment, intimidation, following someone after an event, or sharing someone's location or private info.</li>
        <li><strong>Report anything that feels off.</strong> Tell the host on the spot, jump in our Discord, or email us.</li>
        <li><strong>It's free, and that's the deal.</strong> No fees, no premium tier, no upsell. Venue costs are between you and the venue.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="hp-fine">See the full <a href="/terms">Terms</a> and <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a> pages.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="hp-s" id="account">
      <h2>Account</h2>
      <details class="hp-q">
        <summary>How do I sign in?</summary>
        <div class="hp-a"><p>Go to <a href="/profile/new">/profile/new</a>, enter your email, we send a 6-digit code. Enter it. Done. No password.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="hp-q">
        <summary>What's the difference between Regular and Organizer?</summary>
        <div class="hp-a"><p><strong>Regular</strong> is a private member account — you can RSVP, post community flyers, and host unlimited events. <strong>Organizer</strong> adds a public <code>/u/yourname</code> page with a custom template, booking tools, and group creation. Upgrade anytime from <a href="/profile">/profile</a>.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="hp-q">
        <summary>How do I delete my account?</summary>
        <div class="hp-a"><p>From <a href="/profile">/profile</a>, scroll to the bottom and hit Delete. Wipes your record, RSVPs, photos, and any pages you own. Want a copy of your data first? Email us.</p></div>
      </details>
    </section>

    <footer class="hp-foot">
      <p>Still stuck? <a href="/contact">Send us a message</a> or join our <a href="https://discord.gg/S8SFNkdSgK" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Discord</a>.</p>
    </footer>
  </div>

  <style>
    .hp { max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 48px clamp(20px, 5vw, 32px) 80px; }

    /* Header */
    .hp-h { margin-bottom: 32px; }
    .hp-kicker { font-family: var(--mono, ui-monospace); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-faint); margin-bottom: 12px; }
    .hp-h h1 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(36px, 6vw, 52px); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.05; margin-bottom: 14px; }
    .hp-lede { font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--text-sec); max-width: 56ch; }
    .hp-lede a { color: var(--text); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; }
    .hp-lede a:hover { color: var(--accent); }

    /* TOC — quiet inline */
    .hp-toc {
      display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 16px;
      padding: 14px 0; margin-bottom: 40px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .hp-toc a {
      font-size: 13px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--text-sec);
      text-decoration: none; padding: 4px 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    }
    .hp-toc a:hover { color: var(--text); border-bottom-color: var(--text); }

    /* Sections */
    .hp-s { margin-bottom: 48px; scroll-margin-top: 88px; }
    .hp-s h2 {
      font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin-bottom: 16px;
      padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    /* FAQ — minimal accordion */
    .hp-q { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
    .hp-q:last-of-type { border-bottom: none; }
    .hp-q summary {
      padding: 14px 0; cursor: pointer; list-style: none;
      font-size: 15px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--text);
      display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 16px;
    }
    .hp-q summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
    .hp-q summary::after {
      content: '+'; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 400;
      color: var(--text-faint); flex-shrink: 0;
      transition: transform 0.15s;
    }
    .hp-q[open] summary::after { content: '−'; }
    .hp-q summary:hover { color: var(--accent); }
    .hp-a { padding: 0 0 16px; }
    .hp-a p { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--text-sec); margin: 0 0 10px; }
    .hp-a p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .hp-a a { color: var(--text); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; }
    .hp-a a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
    .hp-a code { background: var(--surface); padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-family: var(--mono, ui-monospace); font-size: 13px; }
    .hp-a strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }

    /* Safety rules — clean list, no boxes */
    .hp-rules { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 16px; }
    .hp-rules li {
      padding: 14px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-sec);
    }
    .hp-rules li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
    .hp-rules strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; display: block; margin-bottom: 2px; font-family: var(--font-display); }
    .hp-fine { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-faint); margin-top: 16px; }
    .hp-fine a { color: var(--text-sec); text-decoration: underline; }

    /* Footer */
    .hp-foot {
      margin-top: 56px; padding-top: 24px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-sec); text-align: center;
    }
    .hp-foot a { color: var(--text); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
    .hp-foot a:hover { color: var(--accent); }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      .hp { padding: 32px 20px 64px; }
      .hp-toc { padding: 12px 0; gap: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 32px; }
      .hp-s { margin-bottom: 36px; }
    }
  </style>
</Base>
